Subject: [PATCH] canvas: opt-in readback noise seeded by the profile

--fingerprint-noise, off by default, adds -1, 0 or +1 to each color
channel of pixels a page reads back from a canvas: getImageData,
toDataURL, toBlob, convertToBlob, ImageBitmap serialization and WebGL
readPixels. The step depends on the profile id, the pixel and its
neighbors, so one profile gives the same bytes on every launch and host,
and alpha never changes. Two profiles on one machine otherwise produce
the same canvas hash, which lets a site link them. Without the switch or
a profile id, pixels are stock.

diff --git a/base/base_switches.h b/base/base_switches.h
--- a/base/base_switches.h
+++ b/base/base_switches.h
@@ -19,6 +19,15 @@
 // readable by web content, so carrying it here discloses nothing to a page.
 inline constexpr char kApostateProfile[] = "apostate-profile";
 
+// Apostate: opt in to profile-seeded perturbation of canvas and WebGL pixel
+// readback. OFF by default, and deliberately outside the profile: it trades
+// coherence with a real machine for unlinkability between sessions, which is
+// the operator's call and not the composer's. Effective only in a renderer
+// that also carries a profile with an identity to seed from; without one the
+// output is byte-for-byte stock. A page cannot read the switch, only its
+// effect, which is the point.
+inline constexpr char kFingerprintNoise[] = "fingerprint-noise";
+
 // Delays execution of TaskPriority::BEST_EFFORT tasks until shutdown.
 inline constexpr char kDisableBestEffortTasks[] = "disable-best-effort-tasks";
 
